    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d901">

                <pb facs="0863" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 851.4054/43</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the French Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jusserand</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1919-10-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 21, 1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor further to refer
                    to your note of September 26, 1919, and my reply note of October 9, 1919,<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d901-f1"/> in regard to the proposed bill relative to the
                    marriage of American soldiers and sailors to French women abroad.</p>
                <p>In this connection I beg to inform you that I am now in receipt of a letter from
                    the War Department of this Government, in which it is stated that the draft of
                    the bill referred to in your note of September 26, 1919, has been submitted to
                    Congress with a request for early enactment.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d901-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d901-f1" n="1" xml:id="d901-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d901-f2" n="2" xml:id="d901-f2-content">
                <p>A bill “To regulate the marriage of persons in the military and naval forces of
                    the United States in foreign countries, and for other purposes” (S. 3245, 66th
                    Cong., 2d sess.), passed the Senate Jan. 19, 1920, but was not passed by the
                    House of Representatives.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
